---
description: Implement proper data retention policies and automatic deletion mechanisms
alwaysApply: true
---

data-retention:

- Define clear data retention periods for different data types
- Implement automatic data deletion after retention period
- Document retention policies in privacy policy
- Provide user-initiated deletion mechanisms
- Maintain audit logs of data deletion
- Consider legal hold requirements before deletion
- Implement soft delete with recovery period where appropriate

Retention policy requirements:
- User account data: Delete within 30 days of account closure request
- Session data: Delete after 90 days of inactivity
- Analytics data: Anonymize after 12 months
- Backup data: Include in deletion processes
- Audit logs: Retain for compliance period (typically 3-7 years)

Good implementation:
```javascript
// Scheduled cleanup job
async function cleanupExpiredData() {
  const retentionDate = new Date();
  retentionDate.setDate(retentionDate.getDate() - 90);
  
  await db.sessions.deleteMany({
    lastActivity: { $lt: retentionDate }
  });
}

// User-initiated deletion
async function deleteUserData(userId) {
  await db.users.softDelete(userId);
  await scheduleHardDelete(userId, 30); // 30-day recovery period
}
```

Bad practices:
```javascript
// No retention policy
await db.users.create(userData); // Stored forever

// No deletion mechanism
// Users cannot delete their data
```
